 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a193b9b0e78b8ef676f972aa157aad969c5199806e875ced948029a1a9f71a14","event_uuid":"4873c871-8bf5-4436-8ece-c4fe05592ae5","position":{"commit_sha":"9c9e2a0219fda838805f4e9a6923443c3084750d","position":"1785725164779720001-4873c871-8bf5-4436-8ece-c4fe05592ae5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"4ea225dcbee6b9df1a2ff2524e2a2b44c9337395e1b6e6fbde08f06311e4052a","event_uuid":"b03e756d-2349-42bb-9a74-06752280251e","position":{"commit_sha":"48f6eb973dd39ddec7375e19213ca8b46b5e60ee","position":"1786096040246015001-b03e756d-2349-42bb-9a74-06752280251e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5ca67c02a66366e0d675a06287e5076900d852b36bd2f1aaa1712c16743dd8b8","event_uuid":"f63dd084-72a1-4918-b699-c5c9def7cea3","position":{"commit_sha":"a386ee85085295e6226082f2e762817f21ae6e95","position":"1786387515892473001-f63dd084-72a1-4918-b699-c5c9def7cea3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ab032e22a7164c68d48032d7c5a2aa3878637a30149e1501deef8deac9ef0a73","event_uuid":"18165a81-cbd5-46d8-af2a-0f4a6ea79830","position":{"commit_sha":"21c90fa24d0f804c0dc4d0c264436a448e2d4e05","position":"1786387522002941001-18165a81-cbd5-46d8-af2a-0f4a6ea79830"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Migration research (official guide py.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io/migration/ + real-world compat shims codeofaxel/Kiln mcp_compat.py, mcp-hangar _sdk_compat.py): FastMCP was RENAMED to MCPServer at mcp.server.mcpserver (decorator API unchanged). rebar-specific inventory: (1) mcp_server.py:607 constructor passes host/port/streamable_http_path/transport_security — v2 moves ALL transport params off the constructor onto run()/streamable_http_app(); rebar already wraps mcp.streamable_http_app (line 634, ProxyAuthMiddleware) and has a single run() call site (line 719), so the plumbing fits but the wrap must be re-verified against the v2 app-builder signature. (2) mcp.server.auth + mcp.server.transport_security import paths are UNCHANGED in v2; token_verifier/auth kwargs remain. (3) mcp.types stays as a permanent alias of the new mcp-types dist — ToolAnnotations import unchanged; camelCase ATTRIBUTE access (.outputSchema etc.) breaks but rebar only mentions those in docstrings, not code. (4) Gotchas to test: DNS-rebinding auto-allowlist is now host:port so a bare 'Host: localhost' gets 421 (audit tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py + auth tests); lifespan now runs ONCE per process not per session; sync def tools now run on a worker thread; McpError -> MCPError with positional ctor; sse-starlette floor jumps to >=3; pydantic-settings and httpx no longer pulled in by mcp (check for indirect reliance); scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py:72 imports the old path too. Verdict: mostly-mechanical single-change migration (no compat shim needed since we can drop <2 outright), with design REVIEW (not redesign) needed at: streamable_http_app wrap, 421 host-header behavior in tests, lifespan scope, and the JSON-RPC-error-vs-isError semantics for MCPError raised inside tools. Alternative fastmcp (PrefectHQ, v3.4) is a separate ecosystem — not recommended as a migration target; official-SDK MCPServer port is the converged OSS path.","timestamp":1785724216852840001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Migrate-vs-defer analysis (complements the migration inventory comment): reasons NOT to migrate immediately, all time-limited. (1) New required deps: mcp 2.0 hard-requires opentelemetry-api>=1.28 and an EXACT-pinned mcp-types (couples two dists in uv.lock), and replaces httpx with httpx2 — httpx/httpx-sse and pydantic-settings are no longer pulled in by mcp, so anything relying on them transitively must declare them. (2) sse-starlette floor jumps >=1.6 -> >=3.0 (two majors ride along). (3) Maturity: 2.0.0 shipped 2026-07-28 (days old); early-major regressions likelier than late 1.x, and the v1.x branch officially receives security fixes — our GHSA-9h52-p55h-vw2f DNS-rebinding protection is intact on 1.29. (4) Behavioral audits required beyond renames: lifespan becomes once-per-process (not per-session); sync def tools run on a worker thread; MCPError inside tools becomes a JSON-RPC error instead of isError=true; bare 'Host: localhost' (no port) now 421s under the auto-allowlist. (5) rebar-mcp is consumed externally — smoke-test protocol negotiation against real clients before flipping. RECOMMENDATION: stay on mcp>=1.28.1,<2 for now (already the landed state via ticket 1dfd change 1245); execute this ticket once mcp 2.0.x has a patch release or two rather than migrating on a .0. When executed, the port is mostly mechanical (FastMCP -> MCPServer at mcp.server.mcpserver, decorator API unchanged, auth/transport_security/mcp.types import paths unchanged) with four design-REVIEW points listed in the prior comment; no compat shim needed since we can drop <2 outright. OSS convergence: official-SDK MCPServer port is the standard path; PrefectHQ fastmcp is a separate ecosystem, not a migration target; compat shims (Kiln mcp_compat.py, mcp-hangar _sdk_compat.py) only matter for projects straddling both majors.","timestamp":1785725164779720001}],"created_at":1785713940797246001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"47b86e1b-53eb-4b9c-8fb4-60245011b1a4","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"1dfd-063e-f341-48da"},{"link_uuid":"b03e756d-2349-42bb-9a74-06752280251e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7466-fe00-bfb3-4a71"}],"description":"Dependabot PR #124 bumps mcp 1.29.0 -> 2.0.0, but mcp 2.0 removes the mcp.server.fastmcp module (verified: ModuleNotFoundError) that rebar's MCP server imports (src/rebar/mcp_server.py:512,570,590; src/rebar/_mcp_auth.py:38; src/rebar/_mcp_models.py:287; scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py:72). Migrating is structural work: port to the mcp 2.0 server API (fastmcp equivalents / mcp-types), update the mcp>=1.28.1,<2 constraint in pyproject.toml (mcp + dev extras), .github/workflows/_optionality.yml:105, and amend ADR 0050:28 (keep the GHSA-9h52-p55h-vw2f floor rationale). Validate with tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp*.py and the workflow-schema test. Deferred out of ticket 1dfd per its path-2 decision rule.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","7466-fe00-bfb3-4a71"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"18165a81-cbd5-46d8-af2a-0f4a6ea79830","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"idea","tags":[],"ticket_id":"732b-51df-acf2-477b","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Migrate MCP server to mcp 2.0 (fastmcp removal)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e726eee3-da52-464a-82e7-a0a1b84cd0ba","47b86e1b-53eb-4b9c-8fb4-60245011b1a4","d99cffdf-1d8e-4f4a-8559-1aa301bced22","4873c871-8bf5-4436-8ece-c4fe05592ae5","b03e756d-2349-42bb-9a74-06752280251e","f63dd084-72a1-4918-b699-c5c9def7cea3","18165a81-cbd5-46d8-af2a-0f4a6ea79830"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659620255497001,"uuid":"acea6d96-28f7-4f86-b2c8-49a13671bec1"}